---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";

const EFFECTIVE = "7 November 2026";
const prose =
  "mt-8 text-[15.5px] leading-7 text-muted-foreground [&_a]:underline [&_a]:underline-offset-4 [&_a:hover]:text-foreground [&_code]:rounded [&_code]:bg-muted [&_code]:px-1 [&_code]:font-mono [&_code]:text-[0.9em] [&_code]:text-foreground [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:tracking-tight [&_h2]:text-foreground [&_li]:mt-2 [&_p]:mt-4 [&_strong]:font-medium [&_strong]:text-foreground [&_ul]:mt-4 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What ui.kadal.cc collects: nothing of its own. No accounts, no analytics, no cookies; a theme and package-manager preference in your browser, and the playground's LiveCodes loaded from livecodes.io."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.14em] text-muted-foreground uppercase">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">Effective {EFFECTIVE}</p>

    <div class={prose}>
      <p>
        ui.kadal.cc is a static documentation site for Kadal UI, run by {SITE.seller}, an individual in {SITE.location},
        trading as {SITE.tradingAs} ("we"). There is nothing to sign up for and nothing to buy here, so there is very
        little to say. This page says it anyway, and it will change if the site does.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect: nothing of our own</h2>
      <p>
        The site has no accounts, no forms, no comments and no newsletter. <strong>It runs no analytics</strong>: no page
        counter, no heatmaps, no advertising or tracking scripts, and no cookies. The fonts are served from this site, not
        from a fonts service. If we ever add a visitor count, this page will describe it before it is turned on, and the
        date above will change.
      </p>

      <h2>Browser storage</h2>
      <p>
        Two preferences are kept in your browser's <code>localStorage</code> so they survive a reload: the theme you chose
        (<code>theme</code>, and <code>starlight-theme</code> for the docs) and the package manager you picked for install
        commands (<code>kadal-ui:pm</code>). They never leave your browser, we cannot read them, and clearing site data
        removes them.
      </p>

      <h2>Server logs</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served by <strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong>, which processes your IP address, browser and the pages you
        request in order to deliver the site, rate-limit abuse and keep it secure, and keeps those logs for a short period.
        We do not use them for anything else.
      </p>

      <h2>The playground</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/playground/">playground</a> runs code in your browser with <strong>LiveCodes</strong>, an open-source
        editor loaded from <a href="https://livecodes.io" rel="noopener">livecodes.io</a>. Opening the playground makes
        your browser fetch LiveCodes from them, as it would an image from another site; what that request shows them
        (your IP address and browser) is handled under their own policies, not ours. What you type stays in your
        browser; it is sent nowhere unless you use one of LiveCodes's own share or export features, which say so when you
        do.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other services</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>GitHub</strong>: the repository, issues, Discussions and <a href="/sponsor/">GitHub Sponsors</a>. A
          sponsorship is a payment to GitHub under GitHub's terms; GitHub handles your card and billing details, and we
          receive only your GitHub username, your tier and whether you chose to be listed publicly.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Discord</strong>: the Kadal server, under Discord's terms and privacy policy.</li>
        <li><strong>npm</strong>: the <code>@kadal/ui</code> package page.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>What those services collect once you are there is theirs to describe, not ours.</p>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        If you write to us, we keep the conversation for as long as it takes to answer and for a reasonable time after, so
        we can follow up. Ask and we delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        We hold no personal data about visitors beyond what is described above, so there is little to see, correct or
        delete; the rights are yours all the same. If you are in India, the Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023 gives
        you them; in the EU or UK, the GDPR does. Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will
        answer within 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this page changes in a way that matters, the date above changes with it and the change is noted in the <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.seller}, trading as {SITE.tradingAs}, {SITE.address} · <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
